# {{project_name}}

<!-- stacks:fill One or two sentences on what this app does and who it's for. -->

A Tauri desktop app. Rust crates in `crates/` own the data and behavior, `src-tauri/` is the app shell, and the React frontend in `src/` talks to Rust through a typed transport generated from the Rust types.

## Quickstart

Requires [Rust](https://rustup.rs) (the toolchain in `rust-toolchain.toml` installs on first use), [bun](https://bun.sh), Node (`.node-version`), make, and jq, plus the [Tauri system prerequisites](https://tauri.app/start/prerequisites/) for your OS.

```bash
make install
make dev        # the full app
make dev-web    # the frontend alone in a browser, on mock data
```

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make dev` / `make dev-web` | Full app / frontend on the mock transport |
| `make lint` / `make format` | Check / fix Biome, rustfmt, and clippy |
| `make typecheck` | tsc and cargo check |
| `make test` | Vitest and cargo test |
| `make e2e` | Playwright against the frontend on the mock transport |
| `make bindings` | Regenerate the TypeScript bindings after changing a Rust command or type |
| `make check` | Everything CI runs |
| `make build` | Production app bundle |

Run `make help` for the full list.

## Layout

```
crates/      Rust library crates (no Tauri)
src-tauri/   app shell: commands, channels, windows, capabilities
src/core/    framework-free TypeScript: transport, generated bindings, mock
src/app/     React: routes, components, hooks, stores
tests/       test helpers and Playwright specs
```

